There is no official way to 'load' arrows into the bow. While you are
wielding ('w') the bow, any arrows you throw ('t') are considered to
be fired from the bow. The same applies to crossbows and bolts, and
slings and stones.

The 'Q' command (quiver) makes this simpler for you by allowing you to
put a whole pile of arrows (or anything else for that matter) into a
conceptual 'quiver'; the 'f' command (fire) is equivalent to 't'-ing
whatever ammo is currently quivered.

(Read the Guidebook; it might be dull to read straight through but it
tells you all this sort of thing.)
